## Browser verification: not done, and why

Running the real UI in this worktree needs `node_modules`, which this lane does
not have. Reusing the main tree's modules through a junction was tried and must
NOT be used: Next.js resolves modules through the link to
`../../../../decision-lab-mainline-integration/node_modules/...`, which escapes
the project root, and the React Server Components manifest then fails with
`Could not find the module ...` — a 500 on the case page in BOTH `next dev` and
`next build && next start`.

That junction artefact briefly looked like a product defect in the case page's
`export const runtime = "edge"`. It is not: the same page is identical on main,
and the failure disappears with the junction removed from the equation. Nothing
is wrong with the case route. Recording this explicitly so the false lead is not
inherited.

Installing dependencies requires product-owner approval (section 18), so the
browser pass (screenshots of the stage indicator advancing during a live run) is
pending that approval. The junctions were removed with
`[System.IO.Directory]::Delete(path, false)` — never `Remove-Item -Recurse`,
which follows a junction and would delete the main tree's real dependencies —
and the main tree's `node_modules` were verified intact afterwards.

